response:
 Write a Java method to test the condition in each case.

Here’s the C# version I came up with, which also makes use of the new-in-C#3 string interpolation features. The use of LINQ and lambdas is particularly neat in this case:

public static IEnumerable<string> FindWordsWithO(string[] words)
  return words.Where(word => word.Contains(interpolation("o")))
.OrderBy(word => word).Take(10).ToArray();
